@obverse
1. [aš-šum] ta-ap-pi₂-iš₈-tar₂
#tr.en: [Regarding] Tappi-Ištar,
2. [DUMU].MUNUS# da-šu-ra-tum
#tr.en: [the daughter] of Dašuratum,
3. [ša] el-lu-lum ip-pu-ši-ma
#tr.en: [whom] Ellulum distrained and
4. [aš]-šum# ta-ap-pi₂-iš₈-tar₂
#tr.en: regarding Tappi-Ištar,
5. [a?-na?] da-šu-ra-tum!(|U.DAR|)
#note: I have corrected the last two signs on the line to the sign TUM. The scribe wrote iš₈-tar₂ instead of TUM, but the name should be da-šu-ra-tum. The scribal error derives from the ending of the previous line which preserves the signs iš₈-tar₂.
#tr.en: [to(?)] Dašuratum,
6. [i-n]a* KA₂ %sux diĝir-mah %akk a-na la ṭe₄-he-e-em
#tr.en: [at] the gate of Diĝir-maḫ to not approach
7. [u₃] la a-ha-zi-im
#tr.en: [and] not marry
8. [ni]-iš DINGIR iz-ku-ru
#tr.en: he swore by the life of the god.
9. [U₄].KUR₂.ŠE₃ a-na MU 5.KAM a-na MU 11*.KAM
#note: The sign @akk{U} for the number 10 seems to have two vertical wedges over it.
#tr.en: "For posterity, for 5 years (or) 11 years
10. [DUMU].MUNUS# a-na el-lu-lum
#tr.en: [(my) daug]hter for Ellulum
11. [l]u* a-na-ṣa-ru-u₂-ma
#tr.en: I shall preserve and
12. [a]-na# aš-šu-tim u₃ mu-tu-tim
#tr.en: for marriage and espousal
13. [lu a]-na*#-ad-di-nu-šum-ma
#tr.en: I shall give to him"
14. [ki?-a?-am?] da-šu-ra-tum!(SUM)
#note: I have corrected the last sign on the line to the sign TUM. The scribe wrote ŠUM instead of TUM, but the name should be da-šu-ra-tum. The scribal error derives from the ending of the previous line which preserves the sign ŠUM. This scribal error follows the same pattern as the one noted for o. 5.
#tr.en: [thus(?) did] Dašuratum
$ end of side

@reverse
1. [MU ri]-im#-{d}+suen LUGAL IN.PA₃
#tr.en: swore [by the life] of Rīm-Sîn, the king.
$ 1 line blank
2. [IGI] it-ti-e₂-a-mil-ki GUDU₄ {d}+EN.KI
#tr.en: [Before] Itti-Ea-milkī, the @i{pašīšum}-priest of Ea;
3. [IGI] wa-ra-a-a {lu₂}KURUN.NA
#tr.en: [before] Warāya, the innkeeper;
4. [IGI] im-gur-{d}+suen MUHALDIM
#tr.en: [before] Imgur-Sîn, the cook;
5. [IGI] {d}UTU-ga-mil LUNGA*
#tr.en: [before] Šamaš-gāmil, the brewer;
6. [IGI] {d}+suen-iš-me-a-ni DUMU E₂-u₂-a
#tr.en: [before] Sîn-išmeanni, the son of Bītūya;
7. [IGI] ni-di-it-tum
#tr.en: [before] Nidittum;
8. [IGI] nu-ur₂-{d}MAR.TU
#tr.en: [before] Nūr-Amurru.
$ 2 lines blank
9. [KIŠIB LU₂.INIM].MA.AB.BI-MEŠ
#tr.en: [The seals] of [the witness]es (have been impressed).
$ 1 line blank
10. [ITI? ŠE?.GUR₁₀?.K]U₅?
#tr.en: [Month XII(?)],
11. %sux [mu {giš}tukul {d}en]-lil₂ mu-na-šum₂-ma
#tr.en: [The year: "With the weapon] given to him by [En]lil
12. %sux [unug{ki} mu]-un#-hul-a
#tr.en: he destroyed [Uruk]".
$ end of side

@seal 1
#note: unpublished
1. {d}s[uen-iš-me-a/an]-ni
2. DUMU E₂-u₂-a
3. ARAD {d}NIN.ŠUBUR
$ end of surface